  route: [
    "Mount Quidamortem: Lovakengj minecart to Quidamortem Station (20 coins; free after The Forsaken Tower), or fairy ring BLS then west and up the path in the north-west.",
    "First time on foot: west from Shayziens' Wall through the lizardman settlement. Speak to the Mountain Guide on top once and he opens a two-way shortcut to the wall.",
    "Xeric's talisman with an ancient tablet (1/10 from the chest) unlocks Xeric's Honour — a teleport straight to the top.",
    "Form a team (your clan chat), register it at the recruiting board, and the leader starts the raid on the stairs. Nobody can join after that.",
    "Deaths are safe. You respawn at the start of your current floor; your raid potions stay on the floor where you died.",
  ],
  loot: {
    uniques: [
      { item: "Dexterous prayer scroll", note: "Rigour — 14/60 of uniques" },
      { item: "Arcane prayer scroll", note: "Augury — 14/60" },
      { item: "Twisted buckler", note: "4/60" },
      { item: "Dragon hunter crossbow", note: "4/60" },
      { item: "Ancestral hat", note: "4/60 (top and bottom the same)" },
      { item: "Dinh's bulwark", note: "3/60" },
      { item: "Dragon claws", note: "3/60" },
      { item: "Elder maul", note: "2/60" },
      { item: "Kodai insignia", note: "2/60" },
      { item: "Twisted bow", note: "2/60 — the reason the raid exists" },
      { item: "Olmlet", note: "the pet, rolled only on raids where you receive a unique" },
      { item: "Ancient tablet", note: "1/10 until you have one: the Xeric's Honour teleport" },
      { item: "Metamorphic dust", note: "Challenge Mode inside the time limit, 1/400" },
      { item: "Twisted ancestral colour kit", note: "Challenge Mode inside the time limit, 1/75" },
    ],
    notes: [
      "Every 8,676 team points is a 1% roll at a unique, capped at 65.7% per 570,000 points; extra points roll a second. Higher personal points make it more likely the unique is yours.",
      "No unique: two different rolls on the common table, scaled by your points up to 131,071 — runes, arrows, noted herbs, ores and gems.",
      "A solo normal raid sits around 30,000 points (a few percent at a purple); Challenge Mode roughly doubles points and adds 5,000 per player for a fast time.",
    ],
  },
  tips: [
    "Learn Olm solo with a 4-tick weapon and the 3:0 method: hit the hand three times, step out of his sight before his attack, step back. Once you can count his rotation, 4:1 with a lance skips every special.",
    "In phases 1 and 2 kill the mage hand first: the melee hand stops clenching and your big specs land freely.",
    "At Olm's teleport, remember the odd player out in a trio is never chosen — the other two still have to stack.",
    "Vasa first in the layout? Walk in below 20 hitpoints or with Vengeance and Protect from Magic ready. At full health the blast leaves you with 5.",
    "Muttadiles: the big one's ranged is far worse than its magic. Keep Protect from Missiles up unless you are counting its three-shot pattern.",
    "Challenge Mode (the CM box at the board): every room in a fixed order — Tekton, crabs, ice demon, shamans / Vanguards, thieving, Vespula, tightrope / guardians, Vasa, mystics, muttadiles — with 50% more stats and health on everything except Olm's health. Olm hits 38–41 in a solo. Inside the time limit (1h10 solo, 42 minutes at five) you roll the dust and the colour kit and the team gets 5,000 points a head. It is the version people mean when they say a raid is 'fast'.",
    "The full-layout toggle gives you the Challenge Mode room order at normal difficulty: a good way to learn every room.",
  ],

